    Project Context
It's a Full-Stack MVP service for carpooling called Pathfinder, developed using Java 21, Spring Boot 3, Spring Data JPA, H2 Database, and Lombok.

    Architecture & Patterns
Architecture layers: Controller, Service, Repository. For the MVP, controllers should work directly with JPA entities, avoiding DTOs and mappers (MapStruct) for speed.
Use @Transactional in the service layer to manage transactions effectively.

    Frontend Guidelines
Client side located in src/main/resources/static/index.html. Use JavaScript (fetch API) for interaction with REST-controllers
and styling with Tailwind CSS (CDN) without installing Node.js, React or other bundlers.

    Code Style & Testing
Generate clean code with proper naming conventions, comments, and Javadoc for public methods and using Lombok.
Use JUnit 5 for unit testing and Mockito for mocking dependencies. Write integration tests for REST controllers using MockMvc.

    Database & Data Management
Use H2 in-memory database for development and testing.
